# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the display test (//editor:up_down_test).
#
# Mesa's gallium drivers race on one of their own thread-pool barriers -- pthread_barrier_wait in
# one of its threads against pthread_barrier_destroy in another -- in a software GL stack. Every
# frame of the report is inside libgallium; its threads are created by glfwCreateWindow and reached
# only through the GL calls in editor::initialize and editor::begin_frame. None of the editor's own
# threads take part, and GL/GLFW are deliberately out of scope for the memory and threading tenets
# (see CLAUDE.md).
#
# Seen on ubuntu-24.04 runners with libgallium 25.2.8, whose version is part of the library's file
# name, so match any version. This does mean a race between first-party code and Mesa would be
# suppressed too; narrow it if that ever becomes a concern.
race:*libgallium*
